  "template_semantics": "Reads the demonstration pairs as context (the pairs that the query is NOT part of). From them it builds, for every input colour b seen at some pixel, the distribution V[b] over the output colours that appeared at those pixels. A query pixel of colour a attends to the seen colours: weight w_b = exp(temp * sim[a][b]) over seen b, normalised; logits = sum_b w_b V[b] + keep * onehot(a); the pixel becomes argmax(logits). So a large diagonal sim copies the demonstrated mapping for colour a, and keep decides when an unseen colour stays unchanged (keep must be below the confidence of a seen mapping, which is about 1, yet above the diluted average used for unseen colours).",
